## PageView linkage targets (Rule 6)

Phase 0 item `i` produced this candidate list. For each, identify which tab/chip row drives the PageView.

| Candidate page | Tab rows detected | Driving row (linkage target) | Auto applies? | Skip reason |
|---|---|---|---|---|
{{PAGEVIEW_LINKAGE_TABLE}}

Driving-row selection rule when 2 rows are present: closer-to-the-list row wins. When ambiguous (both rows equidistant or both filter the same list), Phase 1 surfaces a 4th `AskUserQuestion` (safe mode) or picks closer-to-list default (auto mode).

Skip reasons that opt a candidate out of Rule 6:
- List is one-screen short (PageView between short lists is UX downgrade)
- Filter is binary toggle (use Switch, not PageView)
- Tabs are sectional (form/settings), not data-axis

Each row marked "Skip" must include a reason — empty skip cells abort the plan generation.

